WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.100
The earth has an elegant cycle of life.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.600
It’s the story of carbon.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.940
And over billions of years, it has evolved
to look something like this.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.740
And it starts with a plant.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.820
Plants and microorganisms absorb carbon dioxide
from the atmosphere.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.580
Then they use energy from the sun to convert
that carbon into oxygen…

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.160
And sugar, which they use to grow.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.600
And as they grow, they emit some carbon back
into the atmosphere.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.780
But all plants eventually die.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.420
And some are consumed by bacteria — others
by larger beasts.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.220
These animals eat plants for energy.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.720
And they breathe out carbon.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:55.660
But eventually, those animals die, too.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.380
And they end up in the ground.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.220
Meanwhile, a similar thing happens in the
ocean.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.140
Coral and plankton need carbon from the water
to survive.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.480
Luckily, the ocean has carbon because it absorbs
some from the atmosphere.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.240
And, when rain falls to the earth, it grabs
some carbon from the atmosphere...

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.399
... and from rocks...

00:01:17.399 --> 00:01:21.750
… and flows into the ocean, where the coral
and plankton use carbon to grow.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.760
Or other animals use it to grow.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:28.299
But just like animals, the coral and plankton die, too.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:34.620
In short, all living things are made of carbon
— and they eventually end up in the ground.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.540
Some of that carbon will eventually get back
to the atmosphere.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.820
But some of it normally stays in the ground.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.020
Usually, dead things decay and turn into rocks.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:54.040
Eventually, they’re crushed — and extreme
heat and pressure causes them to melt…

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.920
and emit the carbon, which is trapped
underground.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:03.380
Over time, that trapped carbon eventually
escapes into the atmosphere — when volcanoes

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.200
erupt.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.180
And the cycle starts again.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.860
But occasionally, dead plants and animals
don't turn into rock.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.500
They don't decay fast enough, so they turn into
oil, coal, or natural gas…

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.460
This carbon gets stuck in the ground.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.640
This is the elegant system that keeps carbon
cycling through Earth at a steady pace.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.900
Carbon in the atmosphere keeps some heat from
leaving Earth.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.020
It keeps Earth at a stable temperature.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.760
But very recently, one of these animals started
to dig up the carbon in the ground.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.560
They took the carbon that was stuck in the
ground and put it back into the atmosphere.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:54.000
And they did this so much — in such a short
time span — that this cycle was disrupted.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:58.000
Too much carbon was being put into the atmosphere.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.870
Heat that would normally be able to escape
bounced back and stayed on Earth.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.480
And Earth started to get warmer and warmer.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:12.040
Really recently, just a few months ago,
more than 100 bipedal scientists said they

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.930
might only have 12 years to stop a disastrous
amount of warming.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:22.370
So these animals need to not only stop putting
carbon in the atmosphere, but also get carbon

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.400
out of the atmosphere.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.040
They found that one way to remove carbon is
to grow more plants.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.350
They could stop cutting down trees.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.550
Or raise livestock in ways that help restore
grass.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:37.350
Another way is to let plants suck up carbon
from the atmosphere —

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.240
— but then burn them for energy.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.850
And then trapping the carbon they emit underground.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:49.400
They could also build machines to suck air
from the atmosphere and filter out the carbon.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.500
But they haven't figured out how to do this
fast enough.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:59.430
There are many ways these animals can tweak
this cycle to suck carbon out of the atmosphere.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:04.440
A combination of them is probably the best
way forward.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:10.380
But, first, these animals need to figure out
how to stop putting it there in the first place.

